hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3067","I prayed behing the Prophet ﷺ over a woman who died in childbirth, and he stood opposite her waist. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3195)"
"3068","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the people news of death of Negus on the day on which he died, took them out to the place of prayer, drew them up in rows and said: ""Allah is Most Great"" four times. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3204)"
"3069","“Zaid bin Arqan used to say the Takbir four times in the funeral prayer, and he said the Takbir five times for one funeral. I asked him (about that) and he said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1505)"
"3070","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a dead person, he said: O Allah, forgive those of us who are living and those of us who are dead, those of us who are present and those of us who are absent, our young and our old, our male and our female. O Allah, to whomsoever of us Thou givest life grant him life as a believer, and whomsoever of us Thou takest in death take him in death as a follower of Islam. O Allah, do not withhold from us the reward (of faith) and do not lead us astray after his death. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3201)"
"3071","""I offered the funeral prayer behind Ibn 'Abbas. He recited Fatihat Al-Kitab and a Surah, which he recited loudly, such that we could hear him. When he finished I took him by the hand and asked him. He said: '(It is) Sunnah and the truth.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1987)"
"3072","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) when he recited Surah Al-Fatihah while performing a funeral prayer. When he finished the prayer, I asked him: Did you recite Surah Al-Fatihah? He replied: Yes! O my nephew! This is Sunnah and the truth."
"3073","from the Prophet ﷺ when he prayed during a funeral he would say, “allāhuma ʿabduk, wa-ibnu ʿabdik, kāna yashhadu an lā ilaha illā allāh wa-anna muḥammadun ʿabduka wa-rasūluk, wa-anta aʿlamu bihī minnī, in kāna muḥsinun fa-zid fī iḥsānihi, wa-in kāna musīʾun fa-ighfir lah, wa-lā taḥrimnā ajrah, wa-lā taftinnā baʿdah (O Allah, Your slave and the child of Your female slave is in need of Your mercy, and You are not in need of his torment. If he was pious then increase his rewards and if he was a transgressor then pardon him.)"
"3074","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered the funeral prayer for a man among the Muslims and I heard him say: ‘O Allah, so-and-so the son of so-and-so is in Your case and under Your protection. Protect him from the trial of the grave and the torment of the Fire, for You are the One Who keeps the promise and You are the Truth. Forgive him and have mercy on him, for You are the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1499)"
"3075","""I heard the Messenger of Allah offer the funeral prayer and say: Allahumma ighfir lahu warhamhu waʿfu ʿanhu wa ʿafihi, wa akrim nuzulahu wa wassiʿ mudkhalahu waghsilhu bi-ma'in wa thaljin wa-barad, wa naqqihi min al-khataya kama yunaqqa ath-thawb al-abyad min ad-danas. Wa abdilhu daran khairan min darihi wa ahlan khayran min ahlihi, wa zawjan khayran min zawjihi, wa qihi 'adhab al-qabri wa 'adhab an-nar (O Allah, forgive him and have mercy on him, forgive him and keep him safe and sound, honor the place where he settles and make his entrance wide; wash him with water and snow and hail, and cleanse him of his sin as a white garment is cleansed of dirt. Give him a house better than his house and a family better than his family and a spouse better than his spouse. Protect him from the torment of the grave and the torment of Hell-fire)."" 'Awf said: ""I wished that I was that deceased person because of the supplication that the Messenger of Allah said for that deceased person."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1983)"
"3076","The Prophet ﷺ said: When you pray over the dead, make a sincere supplication for him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3199)"
"3077","The Prophet ﷺ said: When you pray over the dead, make a sincere supplication for him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3199)"
"3078","He who attends the funeral till the prayer is offered for (the dead), for him is the reward of one qirat, and he who attends (and stays) till he is buried, for him is the reward of two qirats. It was said: What are the qirats? He said: They are equivalent to two huge mountains. Two other narrators added: Ibn 'Umar used to pray and then depart (without waiting for the burial of the dead). When the tradition of Abu Huraira reached him, he said:"" We have lost many qirats."" (Using translation from Muslim 945a)"
"3079","The narrator says: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) took pebbles in his fist and began turning them over in his hand, until the messenger returned and informed: Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) has spoken the truth. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) threw the pebbles from his hand towards the ground and said: Then we have lost many qirats."
"3080","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever, with faith and hoping for reward, accompanies a Muslim’s funeral, until the funeral prayer is offered, then remains seated until (the deceased) is placed in the grave, when he returns, he will receive two qirats of reward. Both these qirats are like the mountain of Uhud. And whoever returns after offering the funeral prayer before the burial, he will receive one qirat.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ‘both are like Uhud’ means: one of the two is (as great as) the mountain of Uhud."
"3081","narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a person passes away and a group of one hundred people offer his funeral prayer, and they intercede for him (i.e., pray for his forgiveness), then their intercession is accepted."
"3082","I went outside and found that some people had gathered, so I informed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about it. He asked: “Are there forty people?” I replied: “Yes.” So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: “Bring out his body, for I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘Whenever a Muslim passes away and forty people who do not associate anything with Allah perform his funeral prayer, Allah accepts their intercession for that deceased.’”"
"3083","It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Prophet ﷺ offered the funeral prayer for Najashi and said four Takbir. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1538)"
"3084","That the Prophet prayed at the grave of a woman after she had been buried. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2025)"
"3085","I said to Sha'bi: Who narrated it to you? He said: An authentic one, 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas. This is the word of a hasan hadith. In the narration of Ibn Numair (the words are): The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to the grave which had been newly prepared and prayed over it, and they also prayed who were behind him and he recited four takbirs. I said to 'Amir: Who narrated it to you? He said: An authentic one who saw him, i e. Ibn 'Abbas. (Using translation from Muslim 954a)"
"3086","The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""What happened to so-and-so?"" The people informed him, ""He has passed away."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Why did you not inform me?"" The people had considered his matter insignificant. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to his companions, ""You people come and guide me to his grave."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) went and offered the funeral prayer for that person. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""These graves are dark for their inhabitants, so because of my offering the funeral prayer for them, Allah Almighty illuminates them for them."
"3087","“We went out with the Prophet ﷺ and when we reached Al-Baqi’, we saw a new grave. He asked about it and they said: ‘(It is) so-and-so (a woman).’ He recognized the name and said: ‘Why did you not tell me about her?’ They said: ‘You were taking a nap and you were fasting, and we did not like to disturb you.’ He said: ‘Do not do that; I do not want to see it happen again that one of you dies, while I am still among you, and you do not tell me, for my prayer for him is a mercy.’ Then he went to the grave and we lined up in rows behind him, and he said four Takbir (i.e. for the funeral prayer).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1528)"
"3088","Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"3089","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to a grave, and he (peace be upon him) offered the funeral prayer over it. We performed the funeral prayer behind him, following his lead."
"3090","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to a secluded grave, and he performed the funeral prayer over it. We also performed the funeral prayer behind him. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): In this narration, there is a clear statement: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the funeral prayer over a grave that was in a corner. The word ""manboodh"" means ""corner,"" so these words will guide you to the fact that performing the funeral prayer over a grave is permissible as long as it is new and in a corner that has not been dug up, or among graves that have not been dug up. As for those graves that are dug up and their soil is turned over, their soil becomes impure, and it is not permissible to pray on something impure. However, if a person stands on something clean and then performs the funeral prayer over a grave that has been dug up (then its ruling is different), and this ruling is other than that which is in a corner and has not been dug up."
"3091","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) offered the funeral prayer at the grave of a person who had been buried at night. The Prophet (peace be upon him) and his companions stood up. The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired about this person, so the people informed him: ""So-and-so was buried last night,"" so they offered the funeral prayer (at his grave)."
"3092","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said takbeer four times (while performing the funeral prayer for the deceased)."
"3093","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: A man was wounded, he came to his quiver, took an arrow, and killed himself with it. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not offer his funeral prayer."
"3094","A man from the tribe of Aslam came to the Prophet ﷺ and confessed that he had committed an illegal sexual intercourse. The Prophet ﷺ turned his face away from him till the man bore witness against himself four times. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, ""Are you mad?"" He said ""No."" He said, ""Are you married?"" He said, ""Yes."" Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be stoned to death, and he was stoned to death at the Musalla. When the stones troubled him, he fled, but he was caught and was stoned till he died. The Prophet ﷺ spoke well of him and offered his funeral prayer. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6820)"
"3095","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: A man was wounded, he came to his quiver, took an arrow, and killed himself with it. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not offer his funeral prayer."
"3096","""I was in the second row on the day the Messenger of Allah offered the funeral prayer for An-Najashi."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1974)"
"3097","I was present in the second row at that time."
"3098","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the people news of death of Negus on the day on which he died, took them out to the place of prayer, drew them up in rows and said: ""Allah is Most Great"" four times. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3204)"
"3099","the Messenger of Allah said: ""Your brother has died, so get up and offer the funeral prayer for him."" So we formed two rows for him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1973)"
"3100","It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that the Prophet ﷺ offered the funeral prayer for Najashi and said four Takbir. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1538)"
"3101","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) informed about the death of Najashi on the very day he passed away. The Prophet (peace"
"3102","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) informed us, \""Your brother Najashi has passed away. Stand up and offer his funeral prayer.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, arranged rows behind him, and said four takbirs. People thought as if his body was present in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."""""
"3103","narrates: One day the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon. He mentioned one of his companions who was given a small shroud and was buried at night. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that anyone should be buried at night, except if a person is compelled in this matter (then the ruling is different)."
"3104","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person accompanies a funeral, he should not sit until the body has been placed (in the grave)."
"3105","narrates: Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would go with a funeral, he would not sit down until it was placed in the grave (where the narrator named Abu Muawiyah is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or until it was buried."
"3107","Three things follow the bier of a dead man. Two of them come back and one is left with him: the members of his family, wealth and his good deeds. The members of his family and wealth come back and the deeds alone are left with him. (Using translation from Muslim 2960)"
"3108","I am with you, but when you come to the door of the King (i.e., the True Creator), (meaning when you die), I will leave you and return. These are his family and status. And one friend says: I am with you; wherever you enter and wherever you exit, I am with you. This is his deeds. So that person says: Among these three, you were the least significant in my eyes.”"
"3109","When the Prophet ﷺ placed the dead in the grave, he said: In the name of Allah, and following the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. This is Muslim's version. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3213)"
"3110","The narrator named Abu Sadiq is Bakr bin Qais."
"3111","The narrator says) The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, meant the Muslim and the disbeliever (servant)."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: This narration has been transmitted by Sa'id Maqburi from his father from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, and by Abdur Rahman bin Mehran from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, so both its chains are preserved. The text of the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, is more complete than the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him. We have already mentioned it at the beginning of this chapter.)"
"3112","The grave squeezes (every deceased person); if anyone were to be saved from it, Saad bin Muadh would have been saved from it."
"3113","I may pray.' The angels say: 'You will do that, but tell us about what we have asked you: This man who was among you, what do you say about him, and what testimony do you give about him?' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The person says: 'This is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came with the truth from Allah.' Then it is said to him: 'You lived upon this belief, and you died upon this belief, and if Allah wills, you will be resurrected upon this belief.' Then a door to Paradise is opened for him, and it is said to him: 'This is your place in Paradise, and this is what Allah has prepared for you in Paradise.' So his longing and joy increase. Then a door to Hell is opened before him, and it is said to him: 'If you had disobeyed this (Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this would have been your place, and Allah had prepared these things for you in it.' So his longing and joy increase. Then his grave is expanded for him by seventy cubits, and light is placed for him in the grave. His body is returned to the state in which it began, and then he is placed in a pure body, which is in the form of a bird, hanging from a tree in Paradise. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is what is meant by the saying of Allah: 'Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word, in the worldly life and in the Hereafter...' (to the end of the verse). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the disbeliever is approached from the direction of his head (i.e., the angel tries to come to him), there is nothing there. Then he is approached from his right side, but there is nothing there. Then he is approached from his left side, but there is nothing there. Then he is approached from his feet, but there is nothing there. Then it is said to him: 'Sit up.' So he sits up, frightened and overwhelmed. He is asked: 'What do you say about this man who was among you? What do you say about him, and what testimony do you give about him?' He asks: 'Which man?' Then it is said to him: 'The one who was among you,' but he is not told his name, until it is said to him: 'We are asking about Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).' So the person says: 'I do not know. I heard people saying something, so I said what they said.' Then it is said to him: 'You lived upon this belief, and you died upon this belief, and if Allah wills, you will be resurrected upon this belief.' Then a door to Hell is opened for him, and it is said to him: 'This is your place in Hell, and this is what Allah has prepared for you in Hell.' So his regret and sorrow increase. Then a door to Paradise is opened for him, and it is said: 'If you had obeyed this (Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this Paradise would have been your place, and what Allah has prepared for you in it would have been yours.' So his regret and sorrow increase. Then his grave is constricted for him until his ribs are pressed together. This is the constricted life about which Allah has said: 'Indeed, for him is a constricted life, and We will raise him blind on the Day of Resurrection.'"
"3114","I came to ʿAisha the wife of the Prophet ﷺ during the solar eclipse. The people were standing and offering the prayer and she was also praying. I asked her, ""What is wrong with the people?"" She beckoned with her hand towards the sky and said, ""Subhan Allah."" I asked her, ""Is there a sign?"" She pointed out, ""Yes."" So I, too, stood for the prayer till I fell unconscious and later on I poured water on my head. After the prayer, Messenger of Allah ﷺ praised and glorified Allah and said, ""Just now I have seen something which I never saw before at this place of mine, including Paradise and Hell. I have been inspired (and have understood) that you will be put to trials in your graves and these trials will be like the trials of Ad-Dajjal, or nearly like it (the sub narrator is not sure of what Asma' said). Angels will come to every one of you and ask, 'What do you know about this man?' A believer will reply, 'He is Muhammad, Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he came to us with self-evident truth and guidance. So we accepted his teaching, believed and followed him.' Then the angels will say to him to sleep in peace as they have come to know that he was a believer. On the other hand a hypocrite or a doubtful person will reply, 'I do not know but heard the people saying something and so I said the same.' "" (Using translation from Bukhārī 184)"
"3115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the trial of the grave, so Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Will our intellects be returned to us? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, just as you are today. So he said: There is a restriction on his mouth."
"3116","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the deceased is placed in the grave, it feels as if the sun is about to set, so he says: Let me perform the prayer."
"3117","The Messenger of Allah said: ""When the deceased - or he said when one of you - is buried, two angels, black and blue (eyed_ come to him. One of them is called Al-Munkar, and the other An-Nakir. They say: 'What did you used to say about this man?' So he says what he was saying (before death) 'He is Allah's slave and His Messenger. I testify that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah and that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger.' So they say: 'We knew that you would say this.' Then his grave is expanded to seventy by seventy cubits, then it is illuminated for him. Then it is said to him: 'Sleep.' So he said: 'Can I return to my family to inform them?' They say: 'Sleep as a newlywed, whom none awakens but the dearest of his family.' Until Allah resurrects him from his resting place.""""If he was a hypocrite he would say: 'I heard people saying something, so I said the same; I do not know.' So they said: 'We knew you would say that.' So the earth is told: 'Constrict him.' So it constricts around him, squeezing his ribs together. He continues being punished like that until Allah resurrects him from his resting place."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1071)"
"3118","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the deceased hears even the sound of people's footsteps when they return."
"3119","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said about a command of Allah Almighty (the statement of Allah Almighty is): ""Then for him is a constricted life."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: This refers to the punishment of the grave."
"3120","""When a person is put in his grave and his companions leave him, he hears the sound of their sandals. Two angels come to him, making him sit up, and say to him: 'What did you say about this man (Muhammad)?' As for the believer, he says: 'I bear witness that he says: 'I bear witness that he is the slave of Allah and His Messenger.' It is said to him: 'Look at your place in hell; Allah has replaced it for you with a place better than it.''' The Messenger of Allah said: ""Then he sees them both."" As for the disbeliever or the hypocrite, it is said to him: 'What did you say about this man?' He says: 'I do not know; I used to say what the people said.' It is said to him: 'You did not understand and you did not follow those who had understanding.' Then he is dealt a blow between his ears and the man utters a scream which everything near him hears, except for the two races.''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2051)"
"3121","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Ninety-nine serpents are set upon the disbeliever in his grave, which tear him apart and bite him, and this continues until the Day of Resurrection. If even one of those serpents were to blow upon the earth, the earth would never produce vegetation.”"
"3122","The grave of a believer is a lush garden; his grave is expanded for him up to seventy cubits, and his grave is illuminated for him just like the full moon on the fourteenth night. Do you know about whom this verse was revealed: ""Indeed, for him there will be a constricted life, and We will raise him on the Day of Resurrection blind."" Do you know what is meant by the constricted life? The people said: Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings be upon him, know best. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: It refers to the punishment given to the disbeliever in the grave. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, ninety-nine serpents will be imposed upon him. Do you know what one of those serpents will be? It will be as large as seventy snakes, each snake having seven heads, with which they will bite and tear him, and this will continue until the Day of Resurrection."
"3123",", when she was told that Ibn 'Umar said that the deceased is punished due to the weeping of the living for him, 'Aishah said: ""May Allah forgive Abu 'Abdur-Rahman; he is not lying, but he has forgotten or made a mistake. The Messenger of Allah passed by a (deceased) Jewish woman for whom people were weeping and he said: 'They are weeping for her and she is being punished.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1856)"
"3124","narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him): Once, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) heard a sound at the time of sunset, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is the sound of the Jews who are being punished in their graves."
"3125","I was in a garden of Banu Najjar in which there were some graves of theirs. The Prophet (peace be upon him) was saying: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave. I asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Will there be punishment in the grave? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Yes, people are punished in their graves, which even animals hear."
"3126","I did not fear that you would stop burying one another, I would have asked Allah Almighty to let you hear the punishment of the grave (its sound)."
"3127","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a small leather shield in his hand. He put it down, then he sat behind it and urinated toward it. Some of the people said: 'Look, he is urinating like a woman.' He heard that and said: 'Do you not know what happened to the companion of the Children of Israel? If they got any urine on themselves they would clip that part of their garments off. Their companion told them not to do that and he was punished in his grave.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 30)"
"3128","I have done this so that their punishment may be lightened as long as these do not dry out."
"3129","I have done this) so that their punishment may be lightened as long as these do not dry."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): Mujahid also heard this narration from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he heard it from Tawus on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). So both of its chains are preserved."
"3130","When any one of you dies, he is shown his seat (in the Hereafter) morning and evening; if he is amongst the inmates of Paradise (he is shown the seat) from amongst the inmates of Paradise and if he is one from amongst the denizens of Hell (he is shown the seat) from amongst the denizens of Hell, and it would be said to him: That is your seat until Allah raises you on the Day of Resurrection (and sends you to your proper seat). (Using translation from Muslim 2866a)"
"3131","If you were not (to abandon) the burying of the dead (in the grave), I would have certainly supplicated Allah that He should make you listen the torment of the grave. (Using translation from Muslim 2868)"
"3132","narrates: When Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was wounded, Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) wailed over him, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to her: O Hafsah! Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say that the one over whom wailing is done will be punished? So Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: Yes."
"3133",": "" "" . Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding the statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The punishment of a disbeliever is increased because of the weeping of his family over him."
"3134","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The deceased is punished because of the weeping of the living person."" The narra"
"3135","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿThe deceased is tormented because of the weeping of his family over him.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 315)"
"3136",""" "" : . : : "" "" . : : 164 : "" "" . Ibn Abi Mulaika narrates: I participated in the funeral of Sayyiduna Uthman's son Aban. There, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) arrived and sat down. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) arrived and sat down. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Do you not stop them from crying? I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, the deceased is punished because of the crying of his family over him."" So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) replied to him: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also used to say such a thing. (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrated:) We set out with Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). When we reached the place of Baida, there was a rider under the shade of a tree. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), go and see who this rider is. I went there, and it was Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him). His wife was also with him. She said to me: Call Suhaib to me. Then he joined them, until they reached Madinah Munawwarah. There, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was wounded, so Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Alas, my brother! Alas, my companion! So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Suhaib, do not cry, for I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: The deceased is punished because of the crying of his family over him. Then this matter was mentioned to Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), so she said: By Allah! You are not narrating from liars or those who have been rejected, but for you, the evidence that is in the Qur'an is sufficient, and regarding this, (the command of Allah, the Exalted, is:) ""No bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah increases the punishment of the disbeliever because of the crying of his family over him."
"3137","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this regarding a Jewish woman and her family who were weeping over her: ""These people are weeping, and this woman is being punished in her grave."
"3138","The earth would consume all of the son of Adam except his tailbone. From it he was created, and from it he will be recreated (on the Day of Resurrection). (Using translation from Muslim 2955b)"
"3139","There is a bone in the human being which the earth would never consume and it is from this that new bodies would be reconstituted (on the Day of Resurrection). They said: Messenger of Allah, which bone is that? Thereupon he said: It is the spinal bone. (Using translation from Muslim 2955c)"
"3140","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole body of a human being is consumed by the earth except for a specific part of the backbone."" It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is that thing?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is a thing as small as a mustard seed, through which he will be resurrected."
"3141","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Three practices are from the actions of the Age of Ignorance which the people of Islam have not abandoned: wailing (over the dead), expecting rain to fall because of the stars, and taunting one another."" Rubayyi is the brother of Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah."
"3142","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are four practices from the time of ignorance which people have not abandoned: wailing (over the dead), taunting one another (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words), taunting one another regarding lineage, saying that rain has been sent down upon us by such-and-such star, and believing in contagion (of disease)—if out of a hundred camels, one camel gets scabies, then who caused the first camel to get scabies?"
"3143","Among my people there are four characteristics belonging to pre-Islamic period which they do not abandon: boasting of high rank, reviling other peoples' genealogies, seeking rain by stars, and walling. And he (further) said: If the wailing woman does not repent before she dies, she will be made to stand on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of pitch and a chemise of mange. (Using translation from Muslim 934)"
"3144","Sayyiduna Abu Salama (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, I said:"
"3145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Only for her (you may wail)."""""
"3146","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to take this pledge from women during the oath of allegiance that they would not wail (lament loudly for the dead). The women said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), in the time of ignorance, some women supported us, so that after accepting Islam we would support them. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is no place for (supporting) wailing in Islam. There is no place for shighar (exchange marriage) in Islam. There is no place for ‘aqr (sacrificing camels at the graves of the deceased) in Islam, and there is no place for jalb and janb in Islam. And whoever snatches something, he has no relation with us."
"3147","When the news of the passing of Sayyiduna Zaid bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Ja’far (may Allah be pleased with him),"
"3148","Sayyiduna Ja'far bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) instr"
"3149","“He is not one of us who tears his garments, strikes his cheeks, and cries with the cry of the Days of Ignorance.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1584)"
"3150","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) approached, he instructed: When you carry my funeral, carr"
"3151","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) approached and people began to wail loudly over him, he sa"
"3152","I disassociate myself from that with which the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) disassociated himself, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) disassociated himself from the woman who shaves her head, the woman who wails loudly (at the time of calamity), and the woman who tears her (collar)."
"3153","Sayyiduna Abi (may Allah be pleased with him) hear a man shouting in the manner of the days of ignorance, so he stopped him harshly, although he would not usually do so. Then he said: I think you are confused about this matter, but when I heard him, I could not refrain from saying this, because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever shouts in the manner of the days of ignorance, then you must stop him harshly and do not stop him merely by gesture."
"3154","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has cursed the one who shaves the head, or tears (the collar), or wails loudly."
"3155","The women in the house of Sayyiduna Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) are weeping excessively. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed that man to stop those women from doing so. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: That man went away, then he came back and said: I have stopped them, but they are not listening to me. This happened three times. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Throw dust in their mouths. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I (in my heart) said: May Allah soil your nose with dust; why do you not do what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is telling you?"
"3156","It was narrated from Abu Umamah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who scratches her face and rends her garment and cries that she is doomed (i.e. because of the death of this person). (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1585)"
"3157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Umar! Let them do so, for the eye sheds tears, the body feels pain, and (the distressing event) has just occurred."
"3158","I went with him to his daughter, Sayyida Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), who was breathing her last. Her breath was labored. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whatever Allah takes belongs to Him, and whatever He gives also belongs to Him, and everything has an appointed time. The narrator states: Tears began to flow from the eyes of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon you)! Are you weeping? Did you not forbid weeping? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is mercy, which Allah has placed in the hearts of His servants, and Allah only shows mercy to those of His servants who are merciful."
"3159","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit him along with Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived at his place, he found him in a state of unconsciousness. It was said to him, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! He has passed away.” Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began to weep. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began to weep, the people also began to weep. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Have you not heard that Allah, the Exalted, does not punish because of the weeping of the eye or the grief of the heart, but He punishes or shows mercy because of this”—and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to his tongue."
"3160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He is not from among us; the one who wails has no share (with us). The heart grieves, the eyes shed tears, and we do not say anything except that which does not anger our Lord."
"3161","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three things are equivalent to disbelief in Allah: wailing, tearing the collar, and casting aspersions on lineage."
"3162","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade applying lime to graves. The narrator states: They used the word ""qissah"" for lime."
"3163","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade writing anything on graves.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1563)"
"3164","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade applying lime to graves, writing on them, constructing buildings over them, and sitting on them."
"3165","""The Messenger of Allah forbade plastering over graves, building over them or sitting on them."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2028)"
"3166","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: It is better that one of you should sit on the live coals which burns his clothing and come in contact with his skin than that he should sit on a grave. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3228)"
"3167","“Breaking the bones of the deceased is, in sin, like breaking his bones when he is alive.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1617)"
"3168","I had forbidden you from three things: visiting graves, consuming sacrificial meat for more than three days, and using certain types of vessels except those used for drinking. Now, Muhammad (peace be upon him) has been permitted to visit his mother's grave. I had forbidden you from keeping sacrificial meat for more than three days, and the reason for this was so that those among you who have abundance may give meat to those who have not performed sacrifice. And I had forbidden you from using certain types of vessels except those used for drinking, but a vessel does not make anything lawful or unlawful."
"3169","“The Prophet ﷺ visited the grave of his mother and wept, causing the people around him to weep. Then he said: ‘I asked my Lord for permission to seek forgiveness for her, but He did not give me permission. Then I asked my Lord for permission to visit her grave and He gave me permission. So visit the graves, for they will remind you of death.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1572)"
"3170","I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O son of Khasasiyyah! Have you entered the morning in a state where you have any displeasure with Allah? I replied: I have not entered the morning in a state where I have any displeasure with Allah. Allah has granted me every kind of goodness. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the graves of some polytheists, and he said: These people have gone far ahead of much goodness. He said this three times. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the graves of the Muslims and said: They have attained much goodness. He said this three times. Meanwhile, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept walking, and his gaze fell upon a man who was walking among the graves wearing shoes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out to him in a loud voice: O man with the shoes! Take off your shoes. The man looked, and when he recognized the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he took off his shoes and put them aside. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): It is possible that those shoes were made from the skin of a dead animal that had not been tanned. That is why the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked wearing the skin of a dead animal. And the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “He hears the sound of their shoes when they leave him and return,” contains evidence that entering the graveyard wearing shoes is permissible."
"3171","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the graveyard and said: Peace be upon you, inhabitants of the dwellings who are of the community of the believers. If Allah wills we shall join you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3237)"
"3172","every time it was her night for the Messenger of Allah to stay with her, he would go out at the end of the night to Al-Baqi' and say: ""As-salamu 'alaykum dara qawmin mu'minin, wa inna wa iyyakum mutawa'idun ghadan wa mutawakilun, wa inna in sha' Allahu bikum lahiqun. Allahummaghfir li ahli baqi'il gharaqad. (Peace be upon you, O abode of believing people. You and we used to remind one another about the Day of Resurrection and we are relying on one another (with regard to intercession and bearing witness). Soon we will join you, if Allah willing. O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi' Al-Charqad.)"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2039)"
"3173","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach them, when they went out to the graveyard, to say: As-salamu ‘alaykum ahlad-diyar minal-mu’minina wal- muslimin, wa inna insha’ Allah bikum lahiqun, nas’alul-laha lana wa lakumul-‘afiyah (Peace be upon you, O inhabitants of the abodes, believers and Muslims, and we will join you soon if Allah wills. We ask Allah for well-being for us and for you).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1547)"
"3174","""The Prophet came to 'Abdullah bin Ubayy after he had been placed in his grave, and commanded that he be brought out. He placed him on his knees and blew on him and clothed him in his shirt. And Allah knows best."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2019)"
"3175","""When 'Abdullah bin Ubayy died, his son came to the Prophet and said: 'Give me your shirt so that I may shroud him in it, and (some and) offer the (funeral) prayer for him, and pray for forgiveness for him'. So he gave him his shirt then he said: 'When you have finished, inform me and I will offer the (funeral) prayer for him.' But 'Umar stopped him and said: 'Hasn't Allah forbidden you to offer the (funeral) prayer for the hypocrites?' He said: 'I have two options. Whether you ask forgiveness for them (hypocrites) or ask no forgiveness for them."" So he offered the (funeral) prayer for him. Then Allah, Most High, revealed: 'And never pray (funeral prayer) for any of them (hypocrites) who dies, nor stand at his grave.' So he stopped offering the (funeral) prayer for them."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1900)"
"3176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Leave me, O Umar! When I insisted more, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Leave me, O Umar, for I have been given a choice and I have chosen (what I prefer). Allah the Exalted has said: ""Whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them..."" (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said) If I knew that if I sought forgiveness for him more than seventy times, he would be forgiven, I would do so more than that. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Now I am amazed at my boldness before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). In any case, Allah and His Messenger knew best. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to me, I moved away from him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed his funeral prayer, accompanied his funeral, and stood by his grave until he was buried, then returned. By Allah! Shortly after that, Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: ""And never pray [the funeral prayer] over any of them who dies, nor stand at his grave."" After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) never performed the funeral prayer of any hypocrite, nor did he stand by the grave of any hypocrite."
"3177","We buried a deceased person in the company of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we had finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and we also returned with him. When he approached his door, he stopped, and we saw a woman coming towards him. He (the narrator) said: I think he recognized her. When she went away, we came to know that she was Fatimah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: What brought you out of your house, Fatimah? She replied: I came to the people of this house, Messenger of Allah, and I showed pity and expressed my condolences to them for their deceased relation. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You might have gone to the graveyard with them. She replied: I seek refuge in Allah! I heard you referring to what you mentioned. He said: If you had gone to the graveyard...He then mentioned severe words about it. I then asked Rabi'ah (a narrator of this tradition) about al-kuda (stony land). He replied: I think it means the graves. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3123)"
"3178","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has cursed women who visit graveyards."
"3179","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who visit graves, those who built mosques over them and erected lamps (there). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3236)"
"3180","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who visit graves, those who built mosques over them and erected lamps (there). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3236)"
"3181","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) fell ill, one of his wives mentioned a church which she had seen in the land of Abyssinia. Lady Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) and Lady Umm Habiba (may Allah be pleased with her) had gone to Abyssinia; they mentioned a church which they had seen in the land of Abyssinia, whose name was Maria. They described the beauty of this church and the pictures that were in it. Upon this, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his blessed head and said: It was their custom that when a righteous man among them died, they would build a mosque over his grave and then place his pictures in it. These people are the worst of creatures in the sight of Allah Almighty."
